From 75f84dd13eb1541d0c949ea1d3ef8e160da65ff3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r0ny123 <49360849+r0ny123@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:12:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Give mcritweb and nginx healthchecks, and start nginx
 once mcritweb serves

nginx depended on mcritweb with condition: service_started, which holds as soon as the
container exists, long before gunicorn listens, so nginx answered 502 Bad Gateway for as
long as MCRITweb took to start. Neither service had a healthcheck, so `docker compose ps`
could not say whether either was serving.

mcritweb is now probed with curl on a static file: any HTTP answer counts, as for
mcrit-server, and a static file keeps the probe out of the views (every request still makes
MCRITweb's two small SQLite reads). curl is already in the runtime image. nginx is probed
with `nc -z 127.0.0.1 80`, not HTTP: its server blocks answer 444 to any Host but their
server_name, so an HTTP probe would fail on every deployment that sets its own name. nginx
now waits for mcritweb to be healthy.

Checked with compose v5.1.1, the real nginx image and site configuration, and stand-ins
for the other services, the mcritweb one serving only 20 s after it starts: before, a
client polling once a second got 502 from 13 s to 33 s; after, connection refused until
nginx starts at 33 s and then 200, with all four services reporting healthy. nc -z exits
1 with nothing listening and 0 once nginx is up.
---
 CHANGELOG.md       | 10 ++++++++++
 docker-compose.yml | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 6b85e6c..810f5cc 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -39,6 +39,16 @@ deployment that means saying plainly what an operator has to *do*, which is what
   (default `1`) sets how many run. MCRIT's queue claims a job with one `find_one_and_update` on an
   unset `locked_by`, and each worker has its own UUID, so two workers never take the same job.
 
+### Added
+
+- **Healthchecks for `mcritweb` and `nginx`, and NGINX waits for MCRITweb to serve.** NGINX used
+  to start as soon as the `mcritweb` container existed, and answered `502 Bad Gateway` until
+  gunicorn listened. With a stand-in MCRITweb that takes 20 s to start serving, a client got 502
+  for those 20 s before this change and none after it. `mcritweb` is probed with a static file
+  (any HTTP answer counts, as for `mcrit-server`); `nginx` with a TCP connect, because its server
+  blocks answer 444 to any Host but their `server_name` and an HTTP probe would fail on every
+  deployment that sets one.
+
 ### Upgrading
 
 - The worker container is now named by compose after the project (`docker-mcrit-mcrit-worker-1`
diff --git a/docker-compose.yml b/docker-compose.yml
index 7a9c7d3..f2519d9 100644
--- a/docker-compose.yml
+++ b/docker-compose.yml
@@ -105,6 +105,14 @@ services:
       - ./storage/mcritweb:/opt/mcritweb/instance
     entrypoint:
       - /entry_web_prod.sh
+    healthcheck:
+      # any HTTP answer means gunicorn is serving the app; a static file keeps the probe out of the
+      # views, though every request still makes MCRITweb's two small reads of its SQLite database
+      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "curl -s -o /dev/null http://localhost:5000/static/style.css"]
+      interval: 10s
+      timeout: 5s
+      retries: 10
+      start_period: 30s
     ports: 
       - 127.0.0.1:5000:5000
   nginx:
@@ -114,8 +122,17 @@ services:
     security_opt:
       - no-new-privileges:true
     depends_on:
+      # started is not serving: until gunicorn listens, NGINX answers every request with a 502
       mcritweb:
-        condition: service_started
+        condition: service_healthy
+    healthcheck:
+      # a TCP probe rather than an HTTP one: the server blocks answer 444 to any Host other than
+      # their server_name, so an HTTP probe would fail on every deployment that sets its own
+      test: ["CMD", "nc", "-z", "127.0.0.1", "80"]
+      interval: 10s
+      timeout: 5s
+      retries: 10
+      start_period: 10s
     volumes:
       - ./nginx/nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/nginx.conf:ro
       - ./nginx/uwsgi_params:/etc/nginx/uwsgi_params:ro
